[MATH] within a row the vertical centre of the stepper decrement control = the vertical centre of its value control = the vertical centre of its increment control, to within 1 CSS pixel (BL-UI-005) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] DESKTOP NON-REGRESSION at 768 pixels and above: the mobile full-width stepper rule reverts, the stepper group returns to sharing its product row as a single horizontal group, and no product name is truncated {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the date badge on the long-window card for @td(MSN_PERSKU_ALL.name) is visible carrying the SUCCESS severity, and the warning severity is absent from that badge {SPEC} VCST-5910 plus the Claude Design project frame that declares a comfortable remaining window in success-500 (project id in reports/bugs/open/medium/BUG-loyalty-mission-date-severity-ladder-collapses.md, not repeated here per DV-013) — EXPECTED TO FAIL on the build under test, where success is gated on completion; do not silently correct this assertion to match that
[NEG] that success badge is NOT earned by completion - and this is now stated as a CONTRAST against a live positive exhibit rather than as a bare negative: on the card for @td(MSN_PROGRESS_COMPLETED.name), which IS Completed on the mission-progress-owner identity, a SUCCESS date badge IS present alongside its completion chip, because resolveDateSeverity returns success when isCompleted(mission). So the success token demonstrably ships and is demonstrably reachable - via completion. The claim under test is the OTHER route: the long-window card for @td(MSN_PERSKU_ALL.name) must reach that same success token with NO completion chip present and status @td(MSN_PERSKU_ALL.progress_status), i.e. from the remaining window ALONE, which is what the design requires and what VCST-5910 reports missing. This is the mechanism half of the defect and the sharpest assertion in the case {SPEC} same source; the completion arm is a positive exhibit and never a second expected failure
[REL] POSITIVE CONTROL, passes on the build under test — the severity token on the short-window card for @td(MSN_ENDING_SOON.name) differs from the token on the long-window card, so a failure above is specifically the missing third band and not a badge that never varies at all {OBSERVED}
[NEG] no date badge anywhere in the list carries a severity token outside the declared three-band set {SPEC} same source
[DOM] on each of the two cards the severity is not conveyed by colour alone: the days-left label on that same card is visible and states the remaining window as text, which is the differentiator BL-A11Y-003 and WCAG 1.4.1 require {BL}

[MATH] the currentValue the loyaltyMissionProgress response returns for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.name) = @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.observed_total), the order's grand total — and is NEITHER @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.observed_sub_total) (gross merchandise) NOR @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.predicted_net_merchandise) (merchandise net of discount) {BL}
[REL] DISCRIMINATOR, arm 1 — @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.name) reads Completed. Its target @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.goal_target) sits ABOVE both merchandise readings, so a build that accrued merchandise value of either shape would leave it InProgress; only an order-total accrual completes it {BL}
[REL] DISCRIMINATOR, arm 2 — @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE_NET.name) reads Completed. Its target @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE_NET.goal_target) sits BETWEEN net and gross merchandise, so a build that accrued merchandise NET of discount would leave it InProgress. Arms 1 and 2 together admit exactly one of the three readings, the order total {BL}
[MATH] the discount is not ignored: currentValue = gross merchandise @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.observed_sub_total) plus shipping @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.observed_shipping_total) plus tax @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.observed_tax_total) MINUS discount @td(MSN_PROGRESS_ORDER.observed_discount_total), so a reduction in what the customer actually paid reduced their progress by exactly that amount {BL}
[REL] the currency code carried by the accrued figure on the card for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.name) == @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.goal_currency), the mission's own stored goal currency, and not whichever currency the session happens to carry {BL}
[REL] DECIDABILITY GATE, evaluated before any verdict is recorded — if the response's currentValue for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.name) is 0 or its status is not among InProgress and Completed, the provisioning order never settled against the mission and every arm above is BLOCKED:PRECONDITION_UNMET, never FAIL: that is a data condition and not a product verdict {BL}
[NEG] the literals 'undefined', 'null' and 'NaN' are absent from both cards' progress lines and from both order-goal modals {BL}

[REL] the displayed current figure on the card for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.name) == that mission's TARGET as the response returned it, and is strictly LESS than the raw currentValue the same response returned — the clamp is observable precisely because the raw value is higher {SPEC} source: the display clamps in vc-frontend PR #2471, Math.min(currentValue, target) together with percentage >= 100 ? target : current. Grounded on the PR rather than on a live read; the first run on this identity is what upgrades it
[MATH] the percent rendered on that card = 100, and NOT the raw ratio of currentValue to target that the response supports, which exceeds 100 {SPEC} source: Math.min(percent, 100), same PR
[MATH] the progress-bar fill width on that card divided by its track width = 1.0 within 1 percentage point, and the fill box does not extend beyond the track box on either edge (BL-UI-004) {BL}
[REL] the same three readings hold in the order-goal modal opened from that card, so the clamp is applied on BOTH surfaces rather than only on the card that happened to be verified {SPEC} same source
[REL] LARGER-OVERSHOOT ARM — the same three readings hold for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE_NET.name), whose overshoot over its target is the larger of the two, so a clamp that saturates only just above the target is still caught {SPEC} same source
[NEG] a percent above 100 and the literals 'NaN', 'Infinity' and 'undefined' are absent from both cards and both modals {BL}
[REL] DECIDABILITY GATE, evaluated from the response before any clamp arm is judged — if the raw currentValue is NOT strictly greater than the target for a given mission, that mission's overshoot is gone and its clamp arms are BLOCKED:PRECONDITION_UNMET rather than PASS: with nothing overshooting, clamped and unclamped code render the same thing {BL}

[DOM] the progress-bar fill element on the card for @td(MSN_PROGRESS_COMPLETED.name) carries the completed modifier, and the default in-progress fill class is absent from it {SPEC} source: the &__bar--completed modifier in the mission-card style block, applied on the completed branch
[REL] the computed fill colour of that completed bar == the computed background colour of the 'Completed' success chip on the SAME card, so the bar is painted from the same success token rather than from a second colour that merely resembles it — no colour literal is transcribed into this case {SPEC} same source
[REL] DISCRIMINATOR — that completed fill colour != the computed fill colour of the progress bar on the card for @td(MSN_PROGRESS_PARTIAL.name), which is InProgress. Without this arm, a build that dropped the modifier and painted every bar one colour would still satisfy the assertion above whenever that one colour happened to match the chip {SPEC} same source
